The residue writer and the conflict-marker reader are two halves of one format: format_residue_markers puts divergent anchors in a conflict block before the blank separator and divergent why in a second block after it, and SideBuilder recovers each side's anchor/why boundary from that separator alone. Move the boundary into a conflict block, or infer it from what a line looks like, and ordinary why prose parses as a fabricated anchor while the operator's sentence disappears.
